  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN211.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷatu vēṟupāṭukaṇṭu tōḻi colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said upon seeing the changes in HER who had undergone changes during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN211.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>kēḷā yella tōḻi vāliya</l>
        <l>cutaivirin taṉṉa palpū marā<supplied>a</supplied>m</l>
        <l>paṟaikaṇ ṭaṉṉa pāvaṭi nōṉṟāṭ </l>
        <l>ṭiṇṇilai maruppiṉ vayakkaḷi ṟuriñcutoṟun</l>
        <l>taṇmaḻai yāliyiṟ ṟāa yuḻavar</l>
        <l>veṇṇel vitti ṉaṟaimicai yuṇaṅkum </l>
        <l>paṉipaṭu cōlai vēṅkaṭat tumpar</l>
        <l>moḻipeyar tēetta reṉpa ralkaluṅ </l>
        <l>kuḻiyiṭaik koṇṭa kaṉṟuṭaip perunirai </l>
        <l>piṭipaṭu pūcali ṉeytā toḻiyak </l>
        <l>kaṭuñciṉa vēnta ṉēvali ṉēmati</l>
        <l>neṭuñcē ṇāṭṭiṟ ṟattarap paṭṭa </l>
        <l>kallā veḻiṉi palleṟin taḻuttiya </l>
        <l>vakaṉkaṭ kataviṉ veṇmaṇi vāyiṉ</l>
        <l>mata ṉoṭṭiya kalkeḻu paṉittuṟai</l>
        <l><anchor n="2"/>nīrolit taṉṉa pēe </l>
        <l>ralarnamak koḻiya vaḻappirin tōrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="1a-c">Listen, friend, [my] friend,</l>
        <l corresp="7">beyond Vēṅkaṭam with bedewed groves,</l>
        <l corresp="1d-2c">where many flowers that open like white plaster,</l>
        <l>whenever the strong elephant bull, with solid tusks [and] sturdy legs</l>
        <l corresp="2d-4">with huge feet that look like drums, rubs against the Kadamba tree,</l>
        <l>spread like hail [stones] in a cool rain [and] dry</l>
        <l corresp="5f">on the rocks like the ploughmen’s seeds of white paddy,</l>
        <l corresp="8a-c">in a land where the language is different he is, they say,</l>
        <l>– he who left [me] to cry, while for us great gossip</l>
        <l corresp="16f">stays behind that sounds like the water</l>
        <l corresp="15">at the stony chilly ghat when the strength had shrunk</l>
        <l corresp="14">of the gate of Veṇmaṇi with a wide-spaced door</l>
        <l corresp="13">on which were impressed after the attack the teeth of unlearned Eḻiṉi</l>
        <l corresp="12">who fell when bringing them the far distant land</l>
        <l corresp="11">of Ēmati upon the fiercely angry king’s order</l>
        <l corresp="8d-9">while the big herd, possessing a calf that was held in a pit all night</l>
        <l corresp="10">stayed behind, not reaching [it] through the clamour that came from the elephant cows.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

